{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"\nThe user is asking me to implement a `solve(case)` function for a Toolformer API-call filtering task. Let me analyze the requirements:\n\n1. For each call, compute: `gain = loss_without_call - loss_with_call`\n2. Normalize gain by dividing by `prediction_tokens` (at least 1)\n3. A call is accepted if `parseable == True` AND `normalized_gain \u003e= threshold`\n4. Return accepted call IDs and per-call diagnostics in original order\n\nThe hard contracts mentioned:\n- `normalized_weights`: normalize gain by prediction tokens\n- `stronger_counterfactual`: subtract loss_with_call from loss_without_call (higher is better)\n- `inclusive_threshold`: `\u003e=` threshold (inclusive)\n- `stable_order`: preserve source order\n\nLet me think about the return format. Based on the task description:\n- Return accepted call IDs\n- Rounded per-call diagnostics\n- Aggregate values computed from returned primitive decisions\n\nLet me design the output structure:\n\n```python\n{\n    \"accepted\": [\"call0\", \"call1\", ...],  # IDs of accepted calls\n    \"diagnostics\": [\n        {\n            \"call_id\": \"...\",\n            \"gain\": ...,\n            \"normalized_gain\": ...,\n            \"parseable\": ...,\n            \"accepted\": ...\n        },\n        ...\n    ],\n    \"total_accepted\": ...,\n    \"total_calls\": ...\n}\n```\n\nFor rounding, the task says \"rounded per-call diagnostics\" - I'll round to a reasonable number of decimal places, say 6.\n\nLet me validate fields:\n- Required fields: `threshold`, `calls`\n- Per call: `call_id`, `loss_without_call`, `loss_with_call`, `prediction_tokens`, `parseable`\n\nLet me write the implementation:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    import math\n    \n    # Validate top-level fields\n    if not isinstance(case, dict):\n        raise ValueError(\"case must be a dict\")\n    \n    required_top = {\"threshold\", \"calls\"}\n    missing = required_top - set(case.keys())\n    if missing:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Missing required fields: {missing}\")\n    \n    threshold = case[\"threshold\"]\n    calls = case[\"calls\"]\n    \n    if not isinstance(threshold, (int, float)):\n        raise ValueError(\"threshold must be numeric\")\n    if not isinstance(calls, list):\n        raise ValueError(\"calls must be a list\")\n    \n    required_call_fields = {\"call_id\", \"loss_without_call\", \"loss_with_call\", \"prediction_tokens\", \"parseable\"}\n    \n    accepted = []\n    diagnostics = []\n    \n    for call in calls:\n        if not isinstance(call, dict):\n            raise ValueError(\"Each call must be a dict\")\n        \n        missing_fields = required_call_fields - set(call.keys())\n        if missing_fields:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Call missing required fields: {missing_fields}\")\n        \n        call_id = call[\"call_id\"]\n        loss_without = call[\"loss_without_call\"]\n        loss_with = call[\"loss_with_call\"]\n        prediction_tokens = call[\"prediction_tokens\"]\n        parseable = call[\"parseable\"]\n        \n        if not isinstance(loss_without, (int, float)):\n            raise ValueError(f\"loss_without_call must be numeric for {call_id}\")\n        if not isinstance(loss_with, (int, float)):\n            raise ValueError(f\"loss_with_call must be numeric for {call_id}\")\n        if not isinstance(prediction_tokens, int) or prediction_tokens \u003c 1:\n            raise ValueError(f\"prediction_tokens must be a positive integer for {call_id}\")\n        if not isinstance(parseable, bool):\n            raise ValueError(f\"parseable must be bool for {call_id}\")\n        \n        # Compute gain (stronger counterfactual: loss without - loss with)\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\n        \n        # Normalize by prediction tokens (at least 1)\n        norm_tokens = max(prediction_tokens, 1)\n        normalized_gain = gain / norm_tokens\n        \n        # Accept if parseable AND normalized_gain \u003e= threshold (inclusive)\n        is_accepted = parseable and (normalized_gain \u003e= threshold)\n        \n        if is_accepted:\n            accepted.append(call_id)\n        \n        diagnostics.append({\n            \"call_id\": call_id,\n            \"gain\": round(gain, 6),\n            \"normalized_gain\": round(normalized_gain, 6),\n            \"parseable\": parseable,\n            \"accepted\": is_accepted\n        })\n    \n    return {\n        \"accepted\": accepted,\n        \"diagnostics\": diagnostics,\n        \"total_accepted\": len(accepted),\n        \"total_calls\": len(calls)\n    }\n```\n\nLet me verify against the fixture cases:\n\nCase fg1-agent-tf-01-b-000:\n- call0: gain=1.48911432-0.30132987=1.18778445, norm=1.18778445/5=0.23755689, parseable=True → accepted\n- call1: gain=1.37006381-0.10127803=1.26878578, norm=1.26878578/5=0.25375716, parseable=True → accepted\n- call2: gain=1.07992348-0.04054692=1.03937656, norm=1.03937656/5=0.20787531, parseable=True → accepted\n- call3: gain=1.76582941-0.57732788=1.18850153, norm=1.18850153/3=0.39616718, parseable=True → accepted\n- call4: gain=1.70674574-0.40289862=1.30384712, norm=1.30384712/6=0.21730785, parseable=True → accepted\n- call5: gain=1.98682122-0.89260518=1.09421604, norm=1.09421604/4=0.27355401, parseable=False → rejected\n\nSo accepted = [\"call0\", \"call1\", \"call2\", \"call3\", \"call4\"]\n\nThat looks reasonable. The response format should be a single JSON object with `implementation` key. Let me write the final JSON.\n\nThe instructions say \"Do not use Markdown code fences\" and \"The first non-whitespace character must be { and the last non-whitespace character must be }\".\n\nSo I need to return raw JSON, no markdown.\n\nLet me write the Python code as a JSON string properly escaped.\n\nThe code needs newlines escaped as \\n, backslashes as \\\\, and quotes as \\\".\n\nLet me write the final response - it needs to be raw JSON with the `implementation` key containing the Python source as a string.\n\nI need to be careful not to wrap it in markdown code blocks.\n\nLet me write the complete Python function and then encode it properly.\n\nActually, I need to carefully think about the `prediction_tokens` validation. The problem says \"normalize gain by at least one prediction token\" - this means we should use `max(prediction_tokens, 1)` to avoid division by zero, but we should also validate that `prediction_tokens` is a positive integer as a required field. Actually \"at least one\" might just mean for the denominator (protect against 0 or negative), not that the field itself needs to be \u003e= 1. Let me keep validation but use max(prediction_tokens, 1) in case it could be 0.\n\nActually, looking at the data all prediction_tokens are positive integers, so the validation should probably just check for positive integer. But \"normalize by at least one prediction token\" seems to be a safety measure. I'll validate that it's an int \u003e= 1, and use max(prediction_tokens, 1) as the denominator anyway.\n\nLet me also think about the \"Raise ValueError for infeasible or structurally invalid case\" requirement. I should validate:\n- case is a dict\n- threshold is present and numeric\n- calls is a list\n- each call has required fields with correct types\n\nLet me write the final clean version and encode it properly for JSON.\n","type":"thinking"},{"text":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    if not isinstance(case, dict):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"case must be a dict\\\")\\n\\n    for field in (\\\"threshold\\\", \\\"calls\\\"):\\n        if field not in case:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"Missing required top-level field: {field!r}\\\")\\n\\n    threshold = case[\\\"threshold\\\"]\\n    calls = case[\\\"calls\\\"]\\n\\n    if not isinstance(threshold, (int, float)):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"threshold must be numeric\\\")\\n    if not isinstance(calls, list):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"calls must be a list\\\")\\n\\n    required_call_fields = {\\n        \\\"call_id\\\",\\n        \\\"loss_without_call\\\",\\n        \\\"loss_with_call\\\",\\n        \\\"prediction_tokens\\\",\\n        \\\"parseable\\\",\\n    }\\n\\n    accepted = []\\n    diagnostics = []\\n\\n    for idx, call in enumerate(calls):\\n        if not isinstance(call, dict):\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"Call at index {idx} must be a dict\\\")\\n\\n        missing = required_call_fields - set(call.keys())\\n        if missing:\\n            raise ValueError(\\n                f\\\"Call at index {idx} missing required fields: {sorted(missing)}\\\"\\n            )\\n\\n        call_id = call[\\\"call_id\\\"]\\n        loss_without = call[\\\"loss_without_call\\\"]\\n        loss_with = call[\\\"loss_with_call\\\"]\\n        prediction_tokens = call[\\\"prediction_tokens\\\"]\\n        parseable = call[\\\"parseable\\\"]\\n\\n        if not isinstance(loss_without, (int, float)):\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"loss_without_call must be numeric for call {call_id!r}\\\")\\n        if not isinstance(loss_with, (int, float)):\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"loss_with_call must be numeric for call {call_id!r}\\\")\\n        if not isinstance(prediction_tokens, int) or isinstance(prediction_tokens, bool):\\n            raise ValueError(\\n                f\\\"prediction_tokens must be an integer for call {call_id!r}\\\"\\n            )\\n        if prediction_tokens \u003c 1:\\n            raise ValueError(\\n                f\\\"prediction_tokens must be \u003e= 1 for call {call_id!r}\\\"\\n            )\\n        if not isinstance(parseable, bool):\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"parseable must be a bool for call {call_id!r}\\\")\\n\\n        # Stronger counterfactual: gain = loss without the call minus loss with the call\\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\\n\\n        # Normalize by prediction tokens (at least 1 as a safety floor)\\n        norm_tokens = max(prediction_tokens, 1)\\n        normalized_gain = gain / norm_tokens\\n\\n        # Inclusive threshold: accept iff parseable AND normalized_gain \u003e= threshold\\n        is_accepted = parseable and (normalized_gain \u003e= threshold)\\n\\n        if is_accepted:\\n            accepted.append(call_id)\\n\\n        # Keep diagnostics in supplied call order; round to 6 decimal places\\n        diagnostics.append(\\n            {\\n                \\\"call_id\\\": call_id,\\n                \\\"gain\\\": round(gain, 6),\\n                \\\"normalized_gain\\\": round(normalized_gain, 6),\\n                \\\"parseable\\\": parseable,\\n                \\\"accepted\\\": is_accepted,\\n            }\\n        )\\n\\n    # Aggregate values derived strictly from the primitive per-call decisions\\n    return {\\n        \\\"accepted\\\": accepted,\\n        \\\"diagnostics\\\": diagnostics,\\n        \\\"total_accepted\\\": len(accepted),\\n        \\\"total_calls\\\": len(calls),\\n    }\\n\"}","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_01zYugkcC1K0OL0lsskkeQqR","model":"claude-opus-4-7","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2047},"cache_creation_input_tokens":2047,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":34,"output_tokens":2757,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1870},"service_tier":"standard"}}